SUMMARY:35th Annual Hoes Down Harvest Festival
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 35th Annual Hoes Down Harvest Festival on October 3\, 2026 at Full Belly Farm in Guinda\, California! Held on a real working organic farm in the heart of Capay Valley\, Hoes Down is one of Northern California’s most beloved rural traditions—a joyful celebration of music\, sustainable living\, hands-on learning\, and community connection. \nFrom farm tours and hands-on activities to square dancing\, local organic food\, and camping beneath the walnut orchard—Hoes Down is a place where transformation happens. Kids discover the magic of farm life\, old friends reunite\, and new generations are inspired. \nSince its founding\, Hoes Down has been more than a festival. It is a fundraiser for sustainable agriculture\, rural life\, and community resilience. Last year\, the festival raised nearly $100\,000 for organizations working to strengthen agriculture\, education\, and rural communities. \nTickets are available online only at eco-farm.org. \nFor more information and festival updates\, visit eco-farm.org/hoes-down.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/35th-annual-hoes-down-harvest-festival/
LOCATION:Full Belly Farm\, 15730 County Road 43\, Guinda\, C\, 95637\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bring the Kids,Community,Food & Drink,Music
END:VEVENT
